# HubSpot Private App token. Create one in HubSpot:
# Settings → Integrations → Private Apps.
#
# Full Lifecycle Integrity diagnostic scopes (spell each scope exactly;
# wildcards are not valid):
# crm.objects.contacts.read
# crm.objects.companies.read
# crm.objects.deals.read
# crm.objects.owners.read
# settings.currencies.read
# crm.schemas.contacts.read
# crm.schemas.companies.read
# crm.schemas.deals.read
# automation
# forms
# marketing.campaigns.read
# sales-email-read
# crm.objects.deals.read also covers Deal pipeline/stage reads; HubSpot does
# not expose a separate crm.pipelines.deals.read scope.
#
# HubSpot's automation, forms, and sales-email-read scopes are broader than
# read-only at the platform level. This package accepts them because the
# connector allowlist permits only workflow retrieval/batch-read, Forms GET,
# and CRM email retrieval/search endpoints. Workflow, form, and email writes
# are blocked in code before any network call.
# Without automation the core journey audit can run, but workflow/scoring
# root-cause coverage is explicitly incomplete.
# automation is available only to eligible Professional/Enterprise portals.
# marketing.campaigns.read is available only to Marketing Hub
# Professional/Enterprise portals. If either scope is unavailable, keep the
# remaining readable scopes: the preflight and report disclose the limitation
# and do not convert unavailable evidence into zero activity or a score penalty.
HUBSPOT_PRIVATE_APP_TOKEN=your-read-only-token-here
